// `[]` after a type promises nothing, and a reader who sees brackets expects a constraint. Refused
// rather than ignored, because an empty bracket most likely means somebody deleted the clause and
// left the punctuation — which is exactly the weakening `burxt review` exists to catch, and this
// catches it a step earlier.
function f(n: Int []) -> Int {
    return n;
}
print(f(5));
